rch","description":"Modal advice · internet xavfsizligi","prompt":"Students ___ check the source before sharing information.","text":"Students should check the source before sharing information.","translation":"O‘quvchilar ma’lumotni ulashishdan oldin manbani tekshirishlari kerak.","focus":"should — kerak","words":[{"word":"source","meaning":"manba"},{"word":"sharing","meaning":"ulashish"},{"word":"information","meaning":"ma’lumot"}],"language":"en"}},{"id":"typing:english-15","kind":"typing","title":"B1 · Solving a problem","data":{"id":"b1-5","englishLevel":"B1","level":"B1","title":"Solving a problem","description":"Connected sentence · muammo yechish","prompt":"Although the program failed at first, we found the error and ___ it.","text":"Although the program failed at first, we found the error and fixed it.","translation":"Dastur avval ishlamagan bo‘lsa-da, biz xatoni topib tuzatdik.","focus":"fixed — tuzatdi","words":[{"word":"although","meaning":"garchi"},{"word":"failed","meaning":"ishlamadi"},{"word":"fixed","meaning":"tuzatdi"}],"language":"en"}},{"id":"typing:english-16","kind":"typing","title":"B2 · Effective learning","data":{"id":"b2-1","englishLevel":"B2","level":"B2","title":"Effective learning","description":"Academic vocabulary · ta’lim","prompt":"Regular feedback enables learners to ___ their weaknesses.","text":"Regular feedback enables learners to identify their weaknesses.","translation":"Muntazam fikr-mulohaza o‘quvchilarga zaif tomonlarini aniqlash imkonini beradi.","focus":"identify — aniqlamoq","words":[{"word":"feedback","meaning":"fikr-mulohaza"},{"word":"enables","meaning":"imkon beradi"},{"word":"identify","meaning":"aniqlamoq"}],"language":"en"}},{"id":"typing:english-17","kind":"typing","title":"B2 · Responsible technology","data":{"id":"b2-2","englishLevel":"B2","level":"B2","title":"Responsible technology","description":"Passive voice · texnologiya","prompt":"Personal data must be ___ by strong security rules.","text":"Personal data must be protected by strong security rules.","translation":"Shaxsiy ma’lumotlar kuchli xavfsizlik qoidalari bilan himoyalanishi kerak.","focus":"protected — himoyalangan","words":[{"word":"personal data","meaning":"shaxsiy ma’lumot"},{"word":"protected","meaning":"himoyalangan"},{"word":"security","meaning":"xavfsizlik"}],"language":"en"}},{"id":"typing:english-18","kind":"typing","title":"B2 · Innovation","data":{"id":"b2-3","englishLevel":"B2","level":"B2","title":"Innovation","description":"Complex contrast · yangilik","prompt":"While automation saves time, it also ___ careful human supervision.","text":"While automation saves time, it also requires careful human supervision.","translation":"Avtomatlashtirish vaqtni tejasa-da, u insonning sinchkov nazoratini ham talab qiladi.","focus":"requires — talab qiladi","words":[{"word":"automation","meaning":"avtomatlashtirish"},{"word":"requires","meaning":"talab qiladi"},{"word":"supervision","meaning":"nazorat"}],"language":"en"}},{"id":"typing:english-19","kind":"typing","title":"B2 · Evaluating information","data":{"id":"b2-4","englishLevel":"B2","level":"B2","title":"Evaluating information","description":"Formal instruction · media savodxonligi","prompt":"Before accepting a claim, readers should examine whether the evidence is ___.","text":"Before accepting a claim, readers should examine whether the evidence is reliable.","translation":"Da’voni qabul qilishdan oldin o‘quvchilar dalil ishonchli ekanini tekshirishlari kerak.","focus":"reliable — ishonchli","words":[{"word":"claim","meaning":"da’vo"},{"word":"evidence","meaning":"dalil"},{"word":"reliable","meaning":"ishonchli"}],"language":"en"}},{"id":"typing:english-20","kind":"typing","title":"B2 · Collaborative improvement","data":{"id":"b2-5","englishLevel":"B2","level":"B2","title":"Collaborative improvement","description":"Advanced sentence · loyiha tahlili","prompt":"Had the team tested each component earlier, they would have ___ the problem sooner.","text":"Had the team tested each component earlier, they would have discovered the problem sooner.","translation":"Jamoa har bir qismni oldinroq sinaganida, muammoni tezroq aniqlagan bo‘lardi.","focus":"discovered — aniqladi","words":[{"word":"component","meaning":"tarkibiy qism"},{"word":"discovered","meaning":"aniqladi"},{"word":"sooner","meaning":"tezroq"}],"language":"en"}},{"id":"typing:english-21","kind":"typing","title":"C1 · Careful interpretation","data":{"id":"c1-1","englishLevel":"C1","level":"C1","title":"Careful interpretation","description":"Nuanced vocabulary · tahlil","prompt":"The report should be interpreted with ___, since the sample was relatively small.","text":"The report should be interpreted with caution, since the sample was relatively small.","translation":"Namuna nisbatan kichik bo‘lgani uchun hisobot ehtiyotkorlik bilan talqin qilinishi kerak.","focus":"caution — ehtiyotkorlik","words":[{"word":"interpret","meaning":"talqin qilmoq"},{"word":"caution","meaning":"ehtiyotkorlik"},{"word":"sample","meaning":"namuna"}],"language":"en"}},{"id":"typing:english-22","kind":"typing","title":"C1 · A qualified argument","data":{"id":"c1-2","englishLevel":"C1","level":"C1","title":"A qualified argument","description":"Concession · dalillash","prompt":"___ the proposal has clear benefits, its long-term costs remain uncertain.","text":"Although the proposal has clear benefits, its long-term costs remain uncertain.","translation":"Taklifning aniq foydalari bo‘lsa-da, uning uzoq muddatli xarajatlari noaniqligicha qolmoqda.","focus":"although — garchi","words":[{"word":"proposal","meaning":"taklif"},{"word":"benefit","meaning":"foyda"},{"word":"uncertain","meaning":"noaniq"}],"language":"en"}},{"id":"typing:english-23","kind":"typing","title":"C1 · Research findings","data":{"id":"c1-3","englishLevel":"C1","level":"C1","title":"Research findings","description":"Formal reporting · tadqiqot","prompt":"The findings ___ that regular practice improves both speed and accuracy.","text":"The findings indicate that regular practice improves both speed and accuracy.","translation":"Natijalar muntazam mashq tezlik va aniqlikni oshirishini ko‘rsatadi.","focus":"indicate — ko‘rsatmoq","words":[{"word":"findings","meaning":"natijalar"},{"word":"indicate","meaning":"ko‘rsatmoq"},{"word":"accuracy","meaning":"aniqlik"}],"language":"en"}},{"id":"typing:english-24","kind":"typing","title":"C1 · Constructive review","data":{"id":"c1-4","englishLevel":"C1","level":"C1","title":"Constructive review","description":"Emphasis · fikr bildirish","prompt":"What matters most is not the number of errors, but how effectively they are ___.","text":"What matters most is not the number of errors, but how effectively they are addressed.","translation":"Eng muhimi xatolar soni emas, balki ular qanchalik samarali bartaraf etilishidir.","focus":"addressed — bartaraf etilgan","words":[{"word":"matters","meaning":"ahamiyatli"},{"word":"effectively","meaning":"samarali"},{"word":"addressed","meaning":"bartaraf etilgan"}],"language":"en"}},{"id":"typing:english-25","kind":"typing","title":"C1 · Balanced decision","data":{"id":"c1-5","englishLevel":"C1","level":"C1","title":"Balanced decision","description":"Complex condition · qaror","prompt":"Were the evidence more conclusive, the committee would be ___ to approve the change.","text":"Were the evidence more conclusive, the committee would be inclined to approve the change.","translation":"Dalillar yanada ishonchli bo‘lganida, qo‘mita o‘zgarishni ma’qullashga moyil bo‘lardi.","focus":"inclined — moyil","words":[{"word":"conclusive","meaning":"ishonarli va qat’iy"},{"word":"committee","meaning":"qo‘mita"},{"word":"inclined","meaning":"moyil"}],"language":"en"}},{"id":"typing:english-26","kind":"typing","title":"C2 · Precise distinction","data":{"id":"c2-1","englishLevel":"C2","level":"C2","title":"Precise distinction","description":"Semantic precision · nozik farq","prompt":"The two explanations are not contradictory; they are, in fact, mutually ___.","text":"The two explanations are not contradictory; they are, in fact, mutually complementary.","translation":"Ikki tushuntirish bir-biriga zid emas; aksincha, ular o‘zaro bir-birini to‘ldiradi.","focus":"complementary — bir-birini to‘ldiruvchi","words":[{"word":"contradictory","meaning":"ziddiyatli"},{"word":"mutually","meaning":"o‘zaro"},{"word":"complementary","meaning":"to‘ldiruvchi"}],"language":"en"}},{"id":"typing:english-27","kind":"typing","title":"C2 · Subtle implication","data":{"id":"c2-2","englishLevel":"C2","level":"C2","title":"Subtle implication","description":"Inversion · urg‘u","prompt":"Only after examining the context did the researchers ___ the remark’s significance.","text":"Only after examining the context did the researchers grasp the remark’s significance.","translation":"Tadqiqotchilar faqat kontekstni o‘rgangach, izohning ahamiyatini to‘liq angladilar.","focus":"grasp — to‘liq anglamoq","words":[{"word":"context","meaning":"kontekst"},{"word":"grasp","meaning":"anglamoq"},{"word":"significance","meaning":"ahamiyat"}],"language":"en"}},{"id":"typing:english-28","kind":"typing","title":"C2 · Measured conclusion","data":{"id":"c2-3","englishLevel":"C2","level":"C2","title":"Measured conclusion","description":"Hedging · xulosa","prompt":"The available evidence does not ___ a definitive conclusion, but it points to a clear trend.","text":"The available evidence does not warrant a definitive conclusion, but it points to a clear trend.","translation":"Mavjud dalillar qat’iy xulosaga asos bermaydi, ammo ular aniq yo‘nalishni ko‘rsatadi.","focus":"warrant — asos bermoq","words":[{"word":"warrant","meaning":"asos bermoq"},{"word":"definitive","meaning":"qat’iy"},{"word":"trend","meaning":"yo‘nalish"}],"language":"en"}},{"id":"typing:english-29","kind":"typing","title":"C2 · Elegant reformulation","data":{"id":"c2-4","englishLevel":"C2","level":"C2","title":"Elegant reformulation","description":"Cleft structure · aniq urg‘u","prompt":"It was the clarity of the explanation, rather than its length, that made it so ___.","text":"It was the clarity of the explanation, rather than its length, that made it so compelling.","translation":"Tushuntirishni ta’sirchan qilgan narsa uning uzunligi emas, aynan ravshanligi edi.","focus":"compelling — kuchli va ishontiruvchi","words":[{"word":"clarity","meaning":"ravshanlik"},{"word":"rather than","meaning":"emas, balki"},{"word":"compelling","meaning":"ishontiruvchi"}],"language":"en"}},{"id":"typing:english-30","kind":"typing","title":"C2 · Critical perspective","data":{"id":"c2-5","englishLevel":"C2","level":"C2","title":"Critical perspective","description":"Idiomatic formality · tanqidiy fikr","prompt":"The author stops ___ of dismissing the theory, yet exposes several serious weaknesses.","text":"The author stops short of dismissing the theory, yet exposes several serious weaknesses.","translation":"Muallif nazariyani butunlay rad etmaydi, ammo uning bir nechta jiddiy zaif tomonlarini ochib beradi.","focus":"stop short of — bir ishni qilishgacha bormaslik","words":[{"word":"dismiss","meaning":"rad etmoq"},{"word":"expose","meaning":"ochib bermoq"},{"word":"weakness","meaning":"zaif tomon"}],"language":"en"}},{"id":"typing:long-1","kind":"typing","title":"Uzun matn · Aniq tugmalar","data":{"id":"typing-1","level":"Matn terish","title":"Aniq tugmalar","description":"Qisqa va sodda gap","text":"Men klaviaturada to‘g‘ri o‘tiraman va har bir tugmani shoshilmasdan aniq bosaman.","language":"uz"}},{"id":"typing:long-2","kind":"typing","title":"Uzun matn · Raqamli sinf","data":{"id":"typing-2","level":"Matn terish","title":"Raqamli sinf","description":"Ikki jumlali mashq","text":"Informatika xonasida kompyuterdan tartibli foydalanamiz. Fayllarni kerakli papkaga saqlaymiz, kuchli parol tanlaymiz va internetdagi noma’lum havolalarni ochmaymiz. Tez yozishdan oldin matnni xatosiz yozishga e’tibor beramiz.","language":"uz"}},{"id":"typing:long-3","kind":"typing","title":"Uzun matn · Foydali texnologiya","data":{"id":"typing-3","level":"Matn terish","title":"Foydali texnologiya","description":"Bir abzasli mashq","text":"Kompyuter bizga matn yozish, hisoblash, rasm chizish va yangi bilimlarni o‘rganishda yordam beradi. Dars paytida vazifani diqqat bilan o‘qish, faylga tushunarli nom berish va uni to‘g‘ri joyga saqlash muhim. Klaviaturada ikki qo‘l bilan ishlash yozish tezligini oshiradi. Biroq tezlikning o‘zi yetarli emas: harflar, tinish belgilari va bo‘sh joylar ham aniq kiritilishi kerak. Mashqni muntazam bajargan o‘quvchi vaqt o‘tishi bilan kamroq xato qiladi va fikrini kompyuterda tezroq ifodalay oladi.","language":"uz"}},{"id":"typing:long-4","kind":"typing","title":"Uzun matn · Maktab loyihasi","data":{"id":"typing-4","level":"Matn terish","title":"Maktab loyihasi","description":"Kengaytirilgan matn","text":"Sinfimizda ekologiya mavzusida raqamli loyiha tayyorlashga qaror qildik. Avval har bir guruh o‘z vazifasini belgiladi. Birinchi guruh maktab hovlisidagi daraxtlar haqida ma’lumot to‘pladi, ikkinchi guruh suvdan tejamkor foydalanish bo‘yicha takliflar yozdi, uchinchi guruh esa taqdimot uchun rasmlar tayyorladi. Biz barcha fayllarni bitta papkaga joylab, ularga mazmunini bildiradigan aniq nomlar berdik. Matn yozishda imlo qoidalariga, jumlalarning tushunarli bo‘lishiga va manbalarni ko‘rsatishga e’tibor qaratdik.\n\nKeyin jadval dasturida kuzatuv natijalarini kiritdik. Ustunlarga sana, joy, o‘lchov va izoh yozildi. Diagramma yordamida bir haftadagi suv sarfini taqqosladik. Taqdimot tayyorlashda esa har bir slaydga juda ko‘p matn joylamadik. Sarlavha, qisqa fikr va mavzuga mos rasm ishlatdik. Guruh a’zolari navbat bilan chiqish qilib, bir-biriga muloyim fikr bildirdi. Loyiha yakunida texnologiya faqat tayyor ma’lumotni topish uchun emas, balki muammoni o‘rganish, hamkorlik qilish va foydali yechim yaratish uchun ham kerakligini tushundik.","language":"uz"}},{"id":"typing:long-5","kind":"typing","title":"Uzun matn · Kelajakdagi aqlli maktab","data":{"id":"typing-5","level":"Matn terish","title":"Kelajakdagi aqlli maktab","description":"Yakuniy katta matn","text":"Tasavvur qiling, kelajakdagi maktabga ertalab kirganingizda elektron jadval dars xonalaridagi harorat va yorug‘likni ko‘rsatadi. Bu tizim o‘quvchilarni kuzatish uchun emas, balki qulay muhit yaratish va elektr energiyasini tejash uchun ishlaydi. Sinfdagi sensorlar faqat zarur ma’lumotlarni o‘lchaydi, natijalar esa himoyalangan serverda saqlanadi. O‘qituvchi qurilmalar qanday ishlashini tushuntiradi va har bir o‘quvchi shaxsiy ma’lumotlarni ehtiyot qilish kerakligini biladi.\n\nInformatika darsida guruhlar maktab kutubxonasi uchun kichik dastur yaratadi. Dastur kitob nomi, muallif va mavjud nusxalar sonini ko‘rsatadi. Bir guruh interfeys chizadi, ikkinchi guruh ma’lumotlarni jadvalga kiritadi, yana bir guruh esa xatolarni sinaydi. O‘quvchilar ishni boshlashdan oldin vazifalarni rejalashtiradi. Ular fayllarga tushunarli nom beradi, o‘zgarishlarni alohida nusxalarda saqlaydi va ishlatilgan rasm hamda ma’lumot manbalarini yozib boradi. Agar dasturda muammo chiqsa, ular xatoni yashirmaydi. Avval qaysi qadamda muammo paydo bo‘lganini aniqlaydi, keyin kichik qismlarni navbat bilan tekshiradi.\n\nTanaffusdan so‘ng robototexnika mashg‘uloti boshlanadi. Oddiy robot rangli chiziq bo‘ylab yurishi kerak. O‘quvchilar sensor qiymatini o‘qib, motorlar tezligini boshqaradigan algoritm tuzadi. Dastlab robot burilishda chiziqdan chiqib ketadi. Guruh a’zolari sensorni boshqa joyga o‘rnatib ko‘radi, koddagi tezlikni pasaytiradi va har bir sinov natijasini yozadi. Bir necha urinishdan keyin robot yo‘lni aniq bosib o‘tadi. Bu jarayon ularga muvaffaqiyat birdan kelmasligini, sinov va tahlil yaxshi yechimga olib borishini ko‘rsatadi. Har bir kichik natija keyingi qarorni aniqroq va ishonchliroq qilishga yordam beradi.\n\nKun oxirida o‘quvchilar bajarilgan ishlar haqida qisqa taqdimot qiladi. Ular faqat natijani emas, qaysi usul foydali bo‘lganini va keyingi safar nimani yaxshilash mumkinligini ham aytadi. Tinglovchilar savol beradi, mualliflar esa fikrlarni hurmat bilan qabul qiladi. Shunday maktabda texnologiya darsning maqsadi emas, balki bilim olish vositasi bo‘ladi. Eng muhim ko‘nikmalar qurilma nomlarini yodlash bilan cheklanmaydi. To‘g‘ri savol berish, axborotni tekshirish, xavfsiz ishlash, jamoada kelishish va yaratilgan yechim uchun mas’uliyatni his qilish ham katta ahamiyatga ega. Raqamli vositalardan ongli foydalangan o‘quvchi yangi dastur yoki qurilma paydo bo‘lganda qo‘rqib qolmaydi. U muammoni bosqichlarga ajratadi, o‘rganadi, sinaydi va o‘z fikrini ravon ifodalaydi.","language":"uz"}},{"id":"maze:maze-01","kind":"maze","title":"Birinchi burilish","data":{"id":"maze-01","title":"Birinchi burilish","difficulty":"easy","grid":["###############","#.....#...#...#","#####.#.###.###","#...........#E#","###.#.#####.#.#","#...#.#.#.....#","#.#.#.#.#######","#.#.#.#...#S..#","###.###.#####.#","#.#.....#.#M#.#","#.#.#.###.#.#.#","#.#.#...#.....#","#.#.#.#.#.#.#.#","#...#.#...#.#.#","###############"],"start":[11,7],"exit":[13,3],"monster":[11,9],"route":[[11,7],[13,7],[13,9],[13,11],[11,11],[9,11],[9,13],[7,13],[7,11],[5,11],[5,9],[3,9],[3,7],[3,5],[3,3],[5,3],[7,3],[9,3],[11,3],[11,5],[13,5],[13,3]],"gateCells":[[11,11],[7,13],[5,9],[3,3],[11,3]],"mapSource":"SinfQuiz separately authored fixed layout; see source note in AUDIO-MAZE.md","distance":21,"taskCount":5,"tasks":[{"id":"a1-01","audio":"Turn left at the blue door.","translation":"Ko‘k eshik oldida chapga buriling.","options":["←","↑","→"],"answer":0,"explanation":"“Turn left” chapga burilishni bildiradi.","hints":["Tinglashda yo‘nalish so‘ziga e’tibor bering.","Left — chapga."],"skill":"direction"},{"id":"a1-03","audio":"Turn right after the green tree.","translation":"Yashil daraxtdan keyin o‘ngga buriling.","options":["←","↑","→"],"answer":2,"explanation":"“Turn right” o‘ngga burilishni bildiradi.","hints":["Rangdan keyin kelgan 